      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I can reproduce this, line up some VRCChair3 next to each other, hop between them, look limit angles somehow rotated to some weird angle. It seems to remember your camera rotation relative to the 180 range, and when you sit on a new chair, it rotates you x degree to facing forward, but the 180 range is also rotated by the same x degree when it should not.\n\nE.g. While seated, if you are looking left 22 degrees from forward to click on the new chair, you will sit in the new chair and your camera will reset back to forward (by rotating right 22 degrees), but your new limits are now also rotated to the right 22 degrees, so now you can only look to the left up to 90-22=68 degrees, but your right limit is extended to 90+22=112 degrees.",
